    <desc>Hear or see the bell of a terminal.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Set the bell</title>

<p>Programs ring the bell of the terminal to draw your attention, for example
  when a shell cannot complete what you typed. <app>Pano Terminal</app> can
  play a sound, flash the terminal, or both:</p>
  <steps>
<item><p>Press the menu button in the top-right corner of the window and select <gui style="menuitem">Preferences</gui>.</p></item><item><p>In the <gui>Profiles</gui> group, click the profile you want to change. Its settings open on a page of their own.</p></item>
<item><p>In the <gui>Bell</gui> group, turn <gui>Play a Sound</gui> and <gui>Flash the Terminal</gui> on or off.</p></item>
</steps>

  <p>When the bell rings in a tab in the background, the tab is marked
  instead of flashing.</p>

  <p>To try it, press <keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>G</key></keyseq> at the prompt of a shell.</p>

